0331788063, 0.016462238505482674, 0.008740891702473164, 0.015252380631864071, 0.04056426137685776, -0.013988145627081394, -0.019357744604349136, 0.011500458233058453, -0.029172556474804878, -0.0009141912451013923, 0.0009303340339101851, 0.010181847028434277, -0.010909122414886951, -0.002644017804414034, 0.019942283630371094, 0.013743454590439796], "index": 8, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7277, "total_tokens": 7277}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 771 ---\nComponent: Java Server\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 9 and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7\nDescription: Java Web Tomcat 9 (runtime version 4.103) and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7 (runtime version 1.201) have been updated to Tomcat version 9.0.104.  See the Changelog and Security Fixes.  Recommended action: Update your applications to the latest runtime version. See Keeping Your Application Runtimes Up-to-date.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-28\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 772 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Update Security Recommendation BTP-UAA-0003 for Default Credential Types for Bindings\nDescription: Since 2024-11-12, the default credential type for bindings to service instances of SAP Authorization and Trust Management service has been binding secrets and not instance secrets. We've updated the text of the security recommendation to reflect this fact.  For more information, see BTP-UAA-0003.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-28\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: 2505a\n\n--- Record 773 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: New Parameters for Subaccount Creation in btp CLI and SAP Cloud Management Service API\nDescription: We've introduced two new parameters in the btp create accounts/subaccount command of the btp CLI and in the POST /accounts/v1/subaccounts API of the SAP Cloud Management service for SAP BTP, respectively:      disable-wait-for-auto-assign-plans (btp CLI) / DisableWaitForAutoAssignPlans (API): Allows administrators to specify if the subaccount creation should proceed without waiting for the auto-assignment of base entitlements to complete, which is useful for speeding up the subaccount creation process, particularly in scenarios where quick setup is prioritized over consistency. The default value is false, which is recommended for consistency and reliability, especially when using the command or API to run automated scripts and integrations.      skip-auto-assign-plans (btp CLI) / skipAutoAssignPlans (API): This parameter allows administrators to specify if the subaccount creation should exclude the auto-assignment of base entitlements. If you know in advance that you do not need the base auto-assignments, this offers a quicker subaccount setup and potentially less resource consumption. The default value is false, which includes the base auto-assigned plans.      See btp-create-accounts-subaccount (btp CLI) and POST /accounts/v1/subaccounts (API).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 774 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availability in Additional Regions\nDescription: SAP Document Management Service is now available in the following regions:       Canada (Toronto) (cf-ca20) - Microsoft Azure  Japan (Tokyo) (cf-jp31) - Google Cloud      See information available on the  SAP Discovery Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-28\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 775 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: XSS Detection in PDF Documents\nDescription: We have introduced a new security feature to detect Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities in PDF documents uploaded to the SAP Document Management Service repository. For more information, see Prevention of Persistent XSS Vulnerabilities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-28\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 776 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.40.0\nDescription: The new version brings minor updates for security hardening.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-14\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 777 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: The retirement of Chat and Prompt editor via LLM deployments is complete. Going forward, users will need an orchestration deployment to use the Chat and Prompt Editor apps.  You likely already have an orchestration deployment running. You can check by viewing your deployments in the ML Ops app. For more information, see View a Deployment.  To create a new orchestration deployment, see Create a Deployment for Orchestration.  Alternatively, administrators can use the Enable Orchestration button available through the interface. \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-27\nValid as Of: 2025-05-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record", " your deployments in the ML Ops app. For more information, see View a Deployment.  To create a new orchestration deployment, see Create a Deployment for Orchestration.  Alternatively, administrators can use the Enable Orchestration button available through the interface. \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-27\nValid as Of: 2025-05-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 778 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.17.3\nDescription: We've fixed a bug that caused Istio Operator to create a new ReplicaSet during each reconciliation of a failing, outdated Pod with a sidecar.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-26\nValid as Of: 2025-05-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 779 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configuration API\nDescription: The removeDotsFromMaterialNumber configuration key is now available. The default value is false. Set it to true to remove dots in the extraction results from the string of the following standard line item fields for purchase order documents:  customerMaterialNumber  supplierMaterialNumber     See Create Configuration, Configuration Keys and Extracted Line Items (Base Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-27\nValid as Of: 2025-05-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 780 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Improved ML Model for Purchase Order\nDescription: We’ve improved the machine learning model for purchase order documents.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-27\nValid as Of: 2025-05-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 711 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: GPT-4 versions 0613 and turbo-2024-04-09 and gpt-4-32k version 0613 have been deprecated.  It's recommended that users of these models migrate to GPT-4.1 as a replacement. For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-02\nValid as Of: 2025-06-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 712 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Gemini-1.5-pro and gemini-1.5-flash have been deprecated.    It's recommended that users of these models migrate to gemini-2.0-flash, or gemini-2.0-flash-lite as replacements.   For more information, see SAP Note3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-02\nValid as Of: 2025-06-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 713 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Mistralai--mixtral08x7b-v01 has been deprecated.    It's recommended that users of this model migrate to mistralai--mistral-small-instruct as a replacement.   For more information, see SAP Note3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-02\nValid as Of: 2025-06-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 714 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: An additional module has been added to orchestration.  The translation module translates text, and can be configured for input and output text.  The input translation module helps improve answer quality when the configured model performs better when input is provided in a specific language, for example English.   For more information, see Input Translation and Output Translation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-02\nValid as Of: 2025-06-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 715 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Introduction to CI/CD\nDescription: There is a new chapter that introduces you to Continuous Integration and Delivery (CI/CD), as well as SAP's solution for it.  See Introducing Continuous Integration and Delivery (CI/CD).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-02\nValid as Of: 2025-06-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 716 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4, SAPUI5 version 1.133.4 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2025 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-04\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 717 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change in Navigation for Enabling Analytics AI features\nDescription: A navigation change has been implemented in the SAP Integration Suite for enabling the Analytics AI features. Previously, you had to select Settings  APIs and go to the Analyze tab.  Now, to enable the AI features, such as Anomaly Detection and Predictions:  Navigate to Settings  Artificial Intelligence.  Locate the AI features and switch the toggle button to the ON position.    For more information, see Enabling Anomaly Detection and Predictions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 718 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Role Collections in API Management\nDescription: To provide more flexibility and control in managing API Management entities, we have introduced three new granular role collections:   APIPortal.Configurator  APIPortal.Developer  APIPortal.Tester      Additionally, to restrict a user to managing only API proxies and products—without granting access to policy templates—you can now assign the APIProxy.Developer role.  For more information, see Role Collections in API Management and Comprehensive Breakdown of Role Collections in API Management  SAP API Management customers choose: Role Collections in API Management and Comprehensive Breakdown of Role Collections in API Management\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 719 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:", " and Comprehensive Breakdown of Role Collections in API Management  SAP API Management customers choose: Role Collections in API Management and Comprehensive Breakdown of Role Collections in API Management\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 719 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for API Artifacts Added to Access Policies\nDescription: Support for API artifacts has now been added to access policies. With access policies, unauthorized users can view protected resources—such as integration flows—but cannot perform actions like editing, copying, downloading, deleting, simulating the flow, or monitoring its message content. For more information, see Access Policies for API Artifact and Defining Access Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 720 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Custom Connector URL\nDescription: During the onboarding, you can now use a custom connector URL, which replaces the default connector URL to the outside. See Configuring Connector Setup Using the UI.  To enter a custom connector URL, go to Settings  Data Spaces. In the tab Connect to a Data Space, enter a Custom Connector URL that overwrites the Default Connector URL.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n", "--- Record 3701 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.2.0\nDescription: This release of the Istio module contains Istio updated to version 1.20.0. For more information, read Istio 1.20.0 Release Announcement and Upgrade Notes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-08\nValid as Of: 2023-12-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3702 ---\nComponent: Cloud Application Programming Model\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: December Release\nDescription: The December release of the SAP Cloud Application Programming Model is now available.   Highlights:    Type Definitions are open source  SAPUI5 Mass Edit support  Open Telemetry support  … and much more.  See December 2023 release for the CAP framework.   Action: We recommend to adapt the new versions as soon as possible, see Managing Dependencies.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3703 ---\nComponent: Personalized Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code and stability improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-20\nValid as Of: 2023-12-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3704 ---\nComponent: SA